    "collapsible_tabs_i7rBwx": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "question_bmJh66": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is a CBD tincture?",
            "answer": "<p>A CBD tincture is a liquid wellness product made with hemp-derived cannabidiol (CBD) and a carrier oil, such as MCT oil, hemp seed oil, or olive oil. CBD tinctures are commonly used sublingually—placed under the tongue with a dropper—for a simple, customizable daily CBD routine.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_qmDymB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do you use a CBD tincture?",
            "answer": "<p>To use a CBD tincture, fill the dropper to your preferred serving size, place the liquid under your tongue, hold it for 30–60 seconds, and then swallow. You can also mix CBD oil tincture into coffee, smoothies, or food, although sublingual use is a popular method.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_KDgMmq": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much CBD tincture should I take?",
            "answer": "<p>The right CBD tincture serving varies by person, product strength, body size, and individual wellness goals. Start with the suggested serving size on the label, then increase gradually as needed. Always review the product’s supplement facts and consult a healthcare professional if you take medications or have health concerns.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_g4RbU6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does CBD tincture take to work?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD tincture timing can vary depending on metabolism, serving size, food intake, and whether it is taken under the tongue or mixed into food. Many people include CBD oil tinctures in a consistent daily wellness routine to find the serving and schedule that works best for them.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_n3jn6r": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will CBD tincture make you feel high?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD is non-intoxicating and is not intended to produce a high. However, full-spectrum CBD tinctures may contain trace amounts of THC, while broad-spectrum and CBD isolate tinctures are typically made without THC. Check the product label and third-party lab report for cannabinoid details.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_gPAgYA": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between full-spectrum, broad-spectrum, and CBD isolate tinctures?",
            "answer": "<p>Full-spectrum CBD tinctures contain CBD along with other naturally occurring hemp compounds, including trace THC. Broad-spectrum CBD tinctures include a range of hemp-derived cannabinoids and terpenes but are typically formulated without THC. CBD isolate tinctures contain CBD only, making them a straightforward option for customers seeking pure CBD.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        }
      },
